  "name": "arm",
  "$comment": "Plan 9.10 / X-MB2: the planar 2-link arm on the J-MB6 composites. Power chain: GroundPlanar -> Joint1 (Revolute2DCompliant, compliant pivot kt = 1e8 N/m, bt = 1e3 N s/m) -> Link1 (FixedJoint2D to the link-1 centre of mass, x = 0.2 m) -> BodyJ1 (1-junction) with Body1 (RigidBody2D: m = 2 kg, J = 0.02667 kg m^2; its port is the body 1-junction with I + Coriolis + Gravity + Df) and Joint2 (Revolute2DCompliant whose pivot is the elbow, rx = 0.2 m in the link-1 CoM frame) -> Link2 -> Body2 (link 2 + 0.5 kg payload: m = 1.5 kg, J = 0.015, CoM 0.2 m from the elbow). The fixed-base poses are composed from the joint angles (JointPose2D -> ComposePose2D) and feed Body1.g / Body2.g (gravity reads them) and PoseTip (the end effector, 0.3 m along link 2). Drives: MSe(u1)/MSe(u2) from the 1 ms PD + gravity feedforward ArmPD; Ref1/Ref2 step q1 to 0.6 rad and q2 to -0.4 rad at t = 0.2 s.",
